-- title:
--   Q SDD Complete Part Le Slice
-- statement:
--   **Collapsing a slice measurement to its complete part cannot increase qSDD.** Let $\psi$ be a bipartite state, let $F$ be an indexed polynomial family, and fix $x\in\mathbb{F}_q$. Write $\mathcal C_x$ for the complete-part measurement at $x$ and $\mathcal G_x$ for the original slice measurement, with left and right lifts denoted by superscripts $L$ and $R$. Then
--
--   $$
--   \operatorname{qSDD}_\psi(\mathcal C_x^L,\mathcal C_x^R)
--   \le
--   \operatorname{qSDD}_\psi(\mathcal G_x^L,\mathcal G_x^R).
--   $$
--
--   The complete part collapses the slice outcomes to their total operator. This comparison turns self-consistency of the original slice family into the complete-part estimate needed for the G-hat facts.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Pasting.qSDD_completePart_le_slice`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/LionSR/MIPStarRE/blob/f382c801026f53a9efc260fdee707cb35e0adb15/MIPStarRE/LDT/Pasting/Core/CompletePart.lean#L119-L293

